 "sections": [
  {
   "title": "A real defect that did not turn into a gain",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "body": "The observation vector carried only <b>directed-edge frequencies</b>. An agent could not see which pairs it believed <b>confounded</b> &mdash; a claim that is always required for identification, and the subject of the thesis. The greedy baseline reads all three belief channels through <code>cb.claims</code>. So every learned-versus-greedy comparison in this project has run a blindfolded learner against a sighted rule."
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "body": "It surfaced in the deterministic environment, where observation fixes the skeleton and confounding is the <i>only</i> thing interventions resolve, so the handicap is total there and merely severe elsewhere. Verified directly: a pair with bidirected belief 0.36 was absent from the observation while its directed belief 0.32 was present."
    },
    {
     "type": "note",
     "tone": "warn",
     "body": "Against its matched control, supplying the channels changed the result by <b>+0.020 &plusmn; 0.038</b> &mdash; inside noise. The defect is real and demonstrable; fixing it did not measurably help here. Finding a genuine bug does not entail that removing it improves anything, and this one has not yet earned a place in the results."
    }
   ]
  },
