  {
   "title": "Engine: two thresholds beat one",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "text",
     "body": "The single significance threshold gates both skeleton search and interventional orientation, and their error costs are opposite. Splitting them, with orientation held at 0.01:"
    },
    {
     "type": "table",
     "columns": [
      "skeleton threshold",
      "identified",
      "confidently wrong",
      "missed edges",
      "invented"
     ],
     "rows": [
      {
       "cells": [
        "0.01 (current default)",
        "0.253",
        "0.307",
        "15",
        "3"
       ]
      },
      {
       "cells": [
        "0.05",
        "0.253",
        "0.213",
        "9",
        "3"
       ],
       "highlight": true
      },
      {
       "cells": [
        "0.15",
        "0.133",
        "0.227",
        "13",
        "5"
       ]
      }
     ]
    },
    {
     "type": "text",
     "body": "At 0.05 missed edges halve with no increase in invented ones and no rise in type errors &mdash; exactly what the single-knob sweep destroyed. Identification is flat because recovered edges land in <i>unsure</i> rather than <i>right</i>, but confidently-wrong windows fall 9.4 points. Recommended, not yet the default."
    }
   ]
  },
  {
   "title": "Caveats, and what I would not claim yet",
   "blocks": [
    {
     "type": "list",
     "items": [
      "Single seed on the deterministic arms. The differences between reward variants are within seed noise until replicated &mdash; the ceiling comparison is the solid part.",
      "The deterministic environment answers the infinite-data question only. It cannot speak to sample efficiency or robustness; that is what the statistical layer is for.",
      "The belief-channels fix changes obs_size, so it voids old checkpoints and every pre-fix number is a blindfolded-learner number.",
      "Version-space enumeration is bounded by window DENSITY, not variable count: k&nbsp;&le;&nbsp;6 is the usable range, and a dense k=7 window rejected 94% of worlds."
     ]
    }
   ]
  }
 ],
